From 3a950146a4e1c48da7d7526bd0fe039d47b0322f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian <christian@find.xyz>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 12:34:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Small-screen sizes and a compact Wi-Fi password dialog for
 the 800x480 dash

Local, uncommitted edits from the 2026-08-30 settings work, captured now
as a patch (device/brcm/rpi5/patches/packages_apps_Car_Settings/0001):

- res/values/dimens.xml: car-ui-lib overrides (48 dp touch targets, 56 dp
  toolbar, 48 dp list rows, 32 dp icons, smaller paddings and text) and
  compact alert-dialog margins. The toolbar margin, which car-ui-lib also
  uses as the width of the back-arrow container, was 8 dp: the 32 dp arrow
  overflowed the panel's left edge on every Settings page and was hard to
  press (reported 2026-09-06). Now 44 dp with a 4 dp start inset.
- WifiPasswordDialog rewritten as a plain DialogFragment with its own
  compact layout (res/layout/wifi_password_dialog.xml, drawables), because
  the CarUiDialogFragment version did not fit the panel.
- styles/themes: compact dialog button styles.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I679665ab05023e71c6ac4637d7417b0269445942
